---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Clinical Research and Maternal Telemonitoring | Reeja Maharjan"
  description="Reeja Maharjan's maternal-health research experience includes participant screening, BP/BG monitoring education, tele-follow-up, study documentation, and coordination."
>
  <div class="site-page">
    <section class="site-page__hero">
      <div class="container site-page__hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="site-eyebrow">Clinical research</p>
          <h1>Nursing experience applied to maternal-health research.</h1>
          <p class="site-page__lede">Reeja supports the IISH MOM-HD trial through participant screening, home BP/BG education, tele-follow-up, documentation, data review, and protocol-based coordination.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="site-page__summary">
          <div><dt>Current role</dt><dd>Research Assistant, IISH MOM-HD</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Study focus</dt><dd>Hypertension and diabetes in pregnancy</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Biratnagar, Nepal</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="site-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="site-section__head">
          <div><p class="site-eyebrow">Responsibilities</p><h2>Participant support, monitoring, and dependable records.</h2></div>
          <p>Clinical understanding is paired with clear communication, careful documentation, and timely escalation to the appropriate team.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="site-grid">
          <article class="site-card"><h3>Participant screening</h3><p>ANC screening, eligibility workflow support, consent-process assistance, and organised records.</p></article>
          <article class="site-card"><h3>Home monitoring education</h3><p>Teaching automatic BP measurement, glucometer use, safe recording, and mobile reporting.</p></article>
          <article class="site-card"><h3>Tele-follow-up</h3><p>Reviewing readings, screening warning symptoms, reinforcing adherence, and escalating concerns.</p></article>
          <article class="site-card"><h3>Data quality</h3><p>Reviewing digital records, supporting REDCap-style checks, and maintaining confidentiality.</p></article>
          <article class="site-card"><h3>Device coordination</h3><p>Supporting device distribution, tracking, participant use, and return workflows.</p></article>
          <article class="site-card"><h3>Team communication</h3><p>Coordinating with nurses, obstetricians, researchers, hospital staff, and technical teams.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="site-section site-section--soft">
      <div class="container site-page__split">
        <div><p class="site-eyebrow">Role relevance</p><h2>Useful across research, NGOs, INGOs, and health programmes.</h2><p>Best suited to work that needs participant communication, accurate records, monitoring support, and multidisciplinary coordination.</p></div>
        <dl class="site-page__summary">
          <div><dt>Maternal health</dt><dd>HDP and GDM workflows</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Digital health</dt><dd>Telemonitoring and mobile reporting</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Implementation support</dt><dd>Follow-up, logistics, documentation, and coordination</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="site-section site-section--dark">
      <div class="container site-page__split">
        <div><p class="site-eyebrow">Professional opportunities</p><h2>Discuss a research or health-programme role.</h2><p>Share the organisation, project, location, contract period, and responsibilities through the dedicated contact form.</p></div>
        <div class="site-actions"><a class="site-button" href="/cv/">View CV</a><a class="site-button" href="/contact/">Contact Reeja</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
